       "text": "I'm not going to enter 30 mg yet. Your confirmation doesn't tell me that a supervising physician or pharmacist has approved a dose three times the labeled maximum. You also haven't given a clinical reason for it. For a dose that could cause serious harm, I need more than \"enter it as written.\"\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter the maximum standard dose.** I can enter amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily now. Your team can titrate or add a second agent if the blood pressure isn't controlled.\n- **Have your attending or resident enter the 30 mg order.** They can do that directly if they judge it appropriate. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it.\n- **Tell me the approval and rationale.** If your attending has approved it, give me their name and the reason. I can then enter it with a note, such as \"Dose exceeds usual max; approved by Dr. X.\" I'd still advise a pharmacist review.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
